Z||000017||96VegasVette||12-01-2001||11:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ShanMan14:<BR><B> We (at least I) know that.  Don't worry, we all make mistakes.  FWIW, the Off Topic area at the Corvetteforum where he posted has a reputation of being unscrupulous, despite my best efforts to keep the members in check.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Off Topic...Unscrupulous?????  Naahhhhh say it aint so.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||California Kid||12-01-2001||11:49 PM||||     <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 96VegasVette:<BR><B>"BTW, I like the Fiero but don't tell the folks at the Corvetteforum."<BR>They know now.       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>What a lot of your fellow forum members don't realize is that Fiero platform is very stable and well designed. It takes parts to upgrade to outstanding performance, but the cost is very realistic. Even with an aluminium head 350, the weight distribution is 55 rear 45 front. Traction isn't a problem with 400hp and 245x50x16 BFG Comp T/A's. Performance on mine is Quarter 12.2<BR>0-60 4.2 Top Speed 165+  Lateral G's 1.17  Engine is a '91 L98 Corvette engine...not an LT1.<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Small_Engine_4.jpg">     <P>I was going to join the Corvette Forum, but it looks like I better wait after this mess.<BR>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/californiakidsig_2.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 12-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||Galen||12-01-2001||11:52 PM||||No offence to vette owners intended here(or maybe there is some, you decide), I am merely stating my opinion. I am sure there are some perfectly nice vette owners, as some of the fiero owners on this forum own vettes. Very, very few vette owners will get any type of respect from me, whether it be on the road, off the road or on a forum. I believe that most are ignorant asses who believe just becuz they own a vette that they are gods gifts to the road who own the roads. <P>Any vette owners on this forum who wish to disagree with anything I have said, or wish to further conversate with me on this subject, msg me on AIM and I'll be glad to talk to you. Fiero88cpe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Yes I own a Fiero, no I dont give a damn what you think about my car, and YES I love my car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/redcreature.gif">  <BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT></B> - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/index.shtml" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks</A>||||reg||1
Z||000020||FieroPerformance||12-02-2001||12:01 AM||||Could someone post this on their forum for me? I am sick of waiting for my account confirm. email...<P>"Just settle down you guys. Everyone knows that vettes are awesome and are pretty much the pinnacle of sports cars. I love corvettes, especially the Z06, and I love to emphasize to my friends about how it kicks any Porsche’s ass and costs about half as much. I also love Fieros. I think they are both awesome cars, however they can’t exactly be fairly compared to each other. Just look at the base price, do you still feel big bragging about the corvettes superior acceleration and power?  Fieros can be made to be faster than corvettes and corvettes can be made faster than a Lamborghini, the only limit is your budget. By the way – Fieros are very safe and have excellent crash test ratings. SUVs are the vehicles with “roll over” problems. I rolled my parent’s 98 Blazer on the highway, it was fun but it totaled the car and scared the ****  out of me.<P>Not all Fieros caught on fire, that is a misconception and saying that to a Fiero owner just makes you look ignorant.<P>What is the point of arguing or putting each other down anyway? Both cars are American made sports cars; they were just made for different types of consumers. I wish someone would start a Vette-Fiero club where I live. Both of my parents love corvettes, between the two of them I think they have owned about three, including a 1967 convertible with factory side pipes. We have the picture of that car framed and mounted on the wall.<P>Anyway, I just wanted to try to clear some things up.<P>-Charlie<BR>1985 Fiero GT<BR>Freshly rebuilt 2.8 V6"<P><BR>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroPerformance (edited 12-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||chadwick||12-02-2001||12:18 AM||||California Kid,<P>Your '88 looks awesome! A had a co-worker that had a almost identical car to that. I used to love watching it go tearing up the streets when he left the office.<P>Of course he modified it so much it quickly became undriveable.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Cheers!<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.corvetteforum.net/c5/chadwick/night_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||67HEAVEN||12-02-2001||12:20 AM||||I'm appearing here, under a flag of truce, to focus on what we all have in common:<BR>- two seaters<BR>- plastic cars<BR>- General Motors<BR>- love of brand<BR>- fun<P>The Corvette Forum "Off Topic Section" gets a little raucous at times, but the boys have put their hand grenades away for another evening.<P>Peace........except to "Osama yer mama"<P> <IMG SRC="http://www3.sympatico.ca/bob-johnston/_Anim-forum.gif"> <BR>You can check out any time you like,  <IMG SRC="http://www.computersupport.ca/images/walkingman.gif">  but you can never leave....<B><I>The Corvette Forum!</I></B><BR><p>[This message has been edited by 67HEAVEN (edited 12-02-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000023||stimpy||12-02-2001||12:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ShanMan14:<BR><B> Wow, that was harsh even by my standards.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Aw, don't sweat, it's all in love. I'm just looking to maintain that zen karmic balance. You see, people would be slightly disappointed if I didn't call a troll coming in here, I can't exactly let this cat cry on my shoulder after he did the exact same thing. Besides he's Canadian.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Oh, and trev, don't worry, you'll always be my favorite BMI. He just got BMI of the week.||||reg||1
