Z||000037||sloth85GT||12-02-2001||12:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR><B>And hey, they don't have FieroLisa over there,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>[HOMER VOICE]mmmmmmm FieroLisa ahhhhhhh[/HOMER VOICE]<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>Are you a glutton for punishment?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Slap me, spank me and call me Shirley! Oh baby oh baby.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by California Kid:<BR><B>I can't believe you went over there and acted the way you did!! And said the things you said!! Who the heck has a stock V6 runnings 12's??? Do you think anyone is going to believe that?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Okay, I never said that, if I did, then I didn't mean it to come out that way. I meant that there's some guys with the stock block running 12's, I didn't mean totally stock motor, 1FST2M6 is who I meant, he is using a 2.8 correct? Just with a whole lotta nitrous and running 12's.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroPerformance:<BR><B>Just settle down you guys. Everyone knows that vettes are awesome and are pretty much the pinnacle of sports cars. I love corvettes, especially the Z06, and I love to emphasize to my friends about how it kicks any Porsche’s ass and costs about half as much. I also love Fieros. I think they are both awesome cars, however they can’t exactly be fairly compared to each other. Just look at the base price, do you still feel big bragging about the corvettes superior acceleration and power? Fieros can be made to be faster than corvettes and corvettes can be made faster than a Lamborghini, the only limit is your budget. By the way – Fieros are very safe and have excellent crash test ratings. SUVs are the vehicles with “roll over” problems. I rolled my parent’s 98 Blazer on the highway, it was fun but it totaled the car and scared the **** out of me.<P>Not all Fieros caught on fire, that is a misconception and saying that to a Fiero owner just makes you look ignorant.<P>What is the point of arguing or putting each other down anyway? Both cars are American made sports cars; they were just made for different types of consumers. I wish someone would start a Vette-Fiero club where I live. Both of my parents love corvettes, between the two of them I think they have owned about three, including a 1967 convertible with factory side pipes. We have the picture of that car framed and mounted on the wall.<P>Anyway, I just wanted to try to clear some things up.<P>-Charlie<BR>1985 Fiero GT<BR>Freshly rebuilt 2.8 V6"<P><BR>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Couldn't have said it better!<P>And now my reply to everyone:<P>I didn't go there to make them think that the Fiero is the better car between the two. If I did, then it'd be ME smoking the crack! The Vette is better, hands down, I just love my Fiero and wanted others to just hate it less. I didn't say that I wanted every Vette owner to sell his Vette and buy a Fiero. I just wanted to inform these people about the Fiero. Everyone thinks that all of them will just burst into flames on the click of the ignition. Stupid things like that. I just wanted to change some opinions. I guess I did more bad than good. I apologize to all of the Corvette owners. Someone on there said that it was jealousy on my part. No, I'm not jealous, I love my car and am happy with it. I just felt offended by some other comments I read in other posts regarding the Fiero. People bash things without even learning about them, so I figured if I taught them, they wouldn't bash it as much and maybe even grow to respect it. The guys there were too pig headed to realize that and all of a sudden thought that I was saying that the Fiero is a better car than the Vette. I made a mess and apologize to everyone that was offended, that's the opposite outcome that I wanted.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">     <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||1
Z||000038||GTFiero1||12-02-2001||01:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroPerformance:<BR><B><BR>Not all Fieros caught on fire, that is a misconception and saying that to a Fiero owner just makes you look ignorant.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>and pisses the fiero owner off<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000039||jelly2m8||12-02-2001||01:06 AM||||To the Vette guys,<P> I was going to reply on the Corvette forum, and leave a nasty reply.<P> But I did some reading of the posts there, and then saw that some of you guys dropped by here and gave your feedback.<P> Read some good stuff from you guys, and like was stated in a post here, we have inconciderate folks here also.<P> Great to see you here. Fiero and Corvette owners do have alot in common.<BR> <BR> On a side note, one of my biggest supporters when I built my V8 Fiero is a guy that specializes in Corvette parts and restorations. Blair Molands of Molands Corvettes out of Nova Scotia Canada. Don't know if you guys have heard or dealt with him, but he is big time into Vettes.  He does ship quite a bit of parts and buys parts vehicles all over Canada and the U.S.<P> Blair gave me some smoking deals on Vette parts for my V8, becasue he though it was a "wicked" idea. For example he sold me my Tuned port stuff for 400$, versus the 1500$ he usually charges.<P> Again, nice responcesfrom you guys, hope you stay around.<P> All the best<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
