Z||000062||Cliff Pennock||12-02-2001||06:58 AM||||And all this happened while I was asleep?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>I'll tell you guys a little secret. I like Corvettes. I mean, I like them a lot. Of course I like Fieros much better but I like any car with a <B>history</B>. The Fiero and the Corvette are two of the best looking sportscars ever made in the States.<P>We all have our reasons to like one car over the other. But comparing today's Vette against the Fiero is moot. The Vette has had an extra 13 years of development over the Fiero and is by all means the better car now. That said, I still like the Fiero better for my own personal reasons. I like the way the Fiero handles (better than a Vette? No, just different). I like the fact the Fiero is small (in my eyes, the Vette is <B>huge</B>). And I like the fact Fieros are becoming rare.<P>Anyway, I'd like to say welcome to the Vette guys here. I think it would be cool if someday we could organize a get together so we can glance upon each other's car, and maybe get rid of some misconceptions about the cars in the process.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000063||CoolBlue87GT||12-02-2001||07:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>... The Fiero and the Corvette are two of the best looking sportscars ever made in the States.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well said, Amen<BR>||||reg||1
