Z||000082||87fastback||12-03-2001||02:01 AM||||I actually got kind of bored reading both of these threads, but decided I just HAD to jump into this one.<P>I have owned both Vettes and Fiero's (85 Vette, 95 Pace Car Covertible, 85 Fiero GT and my current 87 Fastback).  The 2 cars actually carry alot of similarities, i.e. composite panels, space frames, etc . . .  and including genuine GM rattles!  I loved my Vettes, and I loved my Fiero's.  But the one thing I can say is it si MUCH cheaper to fix uo a Fiero than it is for a Vette.  Have you ever priced even STOCK Vette calipers?<P>With any car you will have biased opinions, just like what you will see on the Chrysler or Ford boards or even the Honda-Toyota type boards.  We all have individuality and we should all feel free to express that.  But outright slamming other peoples rides is not necessary.  Just think what this world would be like if we all drove the same exact car?  It would be pretty boring.<P>So I guess the only thing I can say to the other Vette owners out there is that sure they are nice cars to a point, but too expensive for my blood to play with.  And if you think your cars are SO nice, take a look at some European engineering for a change.<P>By the way, I worked for GM for years and now work for Toyota - but my love affair with the Fiero still lives on!||||reg||10
