Z||000090||FieroKyle||12-04-2001||12:13 AM||||Blackstang, why do you register with the Stang forum. Might have some good ideas on how to make you V6 faster. I am not trying to drive ya away, but may be get you talking with members that have the same car and interests as you. Not trying to drive ya away    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, just a suggestion. I don't mind ya here as long as you don't talk to talk and piss people off.<P>Anyways, further note, I didn't realize there were so many stupid (excuse me), uneducated Corvette owners. I thought most of them were gear heads.<P>Heres a few favorite quotes:<P>"im glad i sold that POS junk fire chicken!!!!"<BR>- GM made a great car. Handled well, really safe, and had decent performance numbers for the price. A few of the 84's caught fire but were soon fixed.<P>"oh and the idea of putting a 350 engine in the back of a fiero just plain SCARES me!!!<BR>thats like strappin a 350 to a go cart!!!!!"<BR>-The Corvette is not really that much bigger than Fiero except in length, and a Corvette can't fly like a bat out of hell? I don't see where a Corvette is THAT much better off.<P>"It was discontinued for a reason."<BR>-Yeah, they didn't sell enough where GM thought it was worth keeping just the 1 model going when it only uses those parts.<P>"Ohhhh I don't know, maybe it's the whole rolling death trap aspect of the car."<BR>-Yeah, and a Corvette is the safest car on the road. Fieros are some of the safest cars from the 80's <P>"When you get your LT1 installed you're going to have the same problem every person who has a powerful engine in a light car has, including Vette owners, and that's traction."<BR>-So your point is? Atleast a Fiero has the engine in the back to weigh down on them a bit.<P>"It's like puting a V8 into go kart!!"<BR>-Yeah, thats why its fun. But of course a Vette is not fast or dangerous. Any car is dangerous of your driving fast enough if it has an Lt1 or not.<P>"Fair enough. Why do you want a Corvette motor then?" <BR>-Who wouldn't want one in their Fiero!<P>"I respect Fierros for economy cars of the 80's and 90's but not for performance cars. Please don't drive your V8 Fierro fast with a passenger in the car, it isn't fair to them. Those cars do not have the wind tunnel time to travel at a high rate of speed."<BR>-Can't spell Fiero, says they are a 90's car. How in the hell would he know anything on windtunnel? If you can afford an Lt1, I am sure you can get a chin spoiler. Other than they aren't too bad at High speeds with the ground effects.<P>"We don't want to hear about slow POS Fieros." <BR>-They are basically a Chevy, made by the same company. Just because its slower than your Vette doesn't mean its slow.<P>"but for a young kids first car, i think its a good low cost choice...."<BR>-This guy said how terrible and dangerous Fieros are and broke down all the time. Yet he is gonna give one of these dangerous cars to his kids.<P>"You were forced into a Fierro given to you from a family member. You want to like it and make the best out of it. That's cool. We've all been there."<BR>-Guess he don't us very well do he!<P>"Do you have any idea what your weight distribution will be once you drop in an LT1?"<BR>-Yeah not much considering the engine weighs only about 50 to 70 lbs more. ABout 45 to 65, still better than a Vette. The beauty of a midengined car. Porsches and Ferraris don't do it for glamour.<P>"And please, never forget that the Corvette is superior to the Fierro by a long shot in every conceivable category."<BR>-Well it should, its a supercar and priced twice as much. No arguement there until we start talking about making up the difference and putting it into a Fiero. <P>"Most Corvette owners are older and a bit wiser, especially when it comes to cars."<BR>-From what I have read, I doubt it, about the same. Because one 19 year old owns one doesn't mean all 19 year olds own one. (I am 16, lol    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) Still we have resources to get info. <P>"This guy hasn't done ANYTHING WRONG. He came here and wondered why vette owners trash on fieros.. And what do people do.. They dump on his fiero and call him a troll! When he defends himself, you guys dump on him more!!! What if you took your Corvette over to a Porsche site, and they called it a low quality flaming piece of poopie, would you be offended? Would you defend your car? Come on guys, get real!!! Didn't your mothers teach you how to treat a guest!?!?<BR>85Fiero, you're  in my book. Don't mind these guys, they haven't had sex since they ran out jergens.."<BR>-I have respect for this guy because he shows his repect for other people. I like people like this.    <P>"I don't see how an entry level wannabe car could cut into the sales of an icon such as the Corvette If anything the Camaro might cut into the sales but I don't see how anyone considering a Corvette would look into buying a Fiero."<BR>-Even hear the term for the Fiero, a poor man's Corvette? How is the Fiero really a wannabe car? I could see more where we were coming from if it had a Ferrari kit on it with duke performance.<P>Ok thats my rants,    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>I love a Corvette, I would probably take one over the Fiero in a heartbeat if one was offered that was in good condition. But its one of the few I would take over a Fiero. Don't get me wrong, I love Vettes, I just hate ignorant people. Sorry that this post was long.<P>Welcome new members, hope your visit here is a peaceful one. I am about sick of people coming in here with false information and bash away. (MR2, Mustang, 300zx, all ricers owners)<P><BR>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokylesig_1.gif">        <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT<P><p>[This message has been edited by FieroKyle (edited 12-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000091||84fierotrevor||12-04-2001||01:31 AM||||There Right the Corvette is faster then the Fiero. <BR>But my friend mike dust's corvvetts all the time in his Viper. And Mike has been dusted by a toyota supra, And there is about 100 other car's faster then that supra i'm sure.<BR>So none of us have the fastest car.<BR>But ares is cheaper to repier.<BR>Also they are saying that we can't afford anything better then a fiero so we try to build it up as a good car when it is acctuly junk.<BR>If that's true then why do some of these meber's here have like 7 or 10 or even 11 fiero's ? they could own 2 corvettes with that amount of money they paid for those and mod's they put into it !<BR>But there right about me If I had the money I would move up to a better car, Like the bmw M3. I would still keep my fiero for fun sake though cuss there fun! like the reson we own them !||||reg||1
Z||000092||California Kid||12-04-2001||01:39 AM||||Kyle...You really let those guys get to you!!! Ya know, everyone's going to have an opinion. Larger forum means more negative feedback, doesn't mean it's correct, just what they happen to think (which you aren't going to change). Kind of like getting into a disagreement with a certain Mustang owner on this forum.<P>The sad thing is that someone from this forum went over there to start with and made a bad showing. A lot of people copped an attitude right from the start. There is still damage done over there in my opinion.<P>The Fiero is a great car if it is prepared right and it will get more attention than the Corvette, mostly because it's rare, it's attractive, and it can be modded to exceed the Corvette (without huge bills or insurance).<P>Even though I can afford to pay cash for a new C06, I don't want one, my GT keeps me very happy. I've even had two different local Corvette owners with 1 year old cars want to trade me even up...I turned them down. &lt;runs into other room and puts flame suit on!&gt;.  Don't get me wrong, the Corvette is a very nice car for the money, but anybody who's been in the work force for a while can buy one (normally used). It just doesn't get the attention at car shows and cruises that a tricked out Fiero would and does (speaking from experience). <P>Cheer up man.....you could be driving an old rusted up Chrysler K car with a 1.8L burning oil.<P>Man I've been a night owl lately, hope I didn't muff this one up too bad!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/californiakidsig_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000093||AusFiero||12-04-2001||03:32 AM||||I just keep laughing about the crash aspect. Fiero or 80s Corvette in an accident. Give me the Fiero anyday.<BR>Just to make some people happy Fieros are worth as much in Australia as a Corvette. A good Fiero that is. I noticed no one has mentioned which goes around the twisties faster.<BR><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000094||FieroKyleatSchool||12-04-2001||02:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by California Kid:<BR><B>Kyle...You really let those guys get to you!!! </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not really, I thought it was funny on what they had said and for the peoplo who didn't read it, look how stupid they really are.<P>People don't get to me that much. I deal with assholes at work, on the road, at school that say the stupidest things and try to talk other people down when they are so incorrect themselves.||||reg||1
